{"qid":"Q1261908","names":["Principality of Pereyaslavl"],"title":"Principality of Pereyaslavl","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Principality of Pereyaslavl (also Pereiaslavl-Russʹkyi) was a frontier principality of Kievan Rus' established around 1054 after the division of the Rus' lands among Yaroslav the Wise's sons, with Vsevolod I receiving Pereyaslavl as his share. Situated on the left bank of the Dnieper south of Chernigov, it bore the brunt of Cuman (Polovtsian) steppe incursions and served as a buffer for Kiev; its princes frequently fought or negotiated with nomadic confederacies. The principality produced no dominant ruling line: it changed hands among various Ryurikid branches throughout the 12th century. Mongol forces destroyed the city of Pereyaslavl in 1239–40, effectively ending the principality as an organized polity.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The principality's core territory is attested in Rus' chronicles, but exact boundaries with neighboring principalities and the steppe frontier are not precisely delimited in sources.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Principality of Pereyaslavl","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principality_of_Pereyaslavl"},{"label":"Britannica: Pereyaslav","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Pereyaslav"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Principality of Pereyaslavl","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Vsevolod I Yaroslavich","nativeName":"Всеволод Ярославич","roman":"Vsevolod I","start":1056,"end":1078,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Rostislav Vsevolodich","nativeName":"Ростислав Всеволодич","ro